A||||3||Cheever2||Anybody familiar with speedcorp.net?||||2||
Z||000000||Cheever2||02-21-2001||06:58 PM||||Heard from people at work about... <A HREF="http://www.speedcorp.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.speedcorp.net/</A> <P>... and before I try anything, I'm wondering if any of you have experience with their stuff.  One question I have is: how do I backup my registry (before installing "tweaks")?  You can tell I don't really know what I'm doing, just want to get the maximum performance I can get.  I wouldn't throw crap on my car without checking the Forum first, and I also shouldn't throw crap on my PC without some advice.  Just use good ol' plain English, please.<BR><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||2
Z||000001||SteveJ||02-21-2001||08:37 PM||||I have spent the last 15 years of my life with computers. My sage advice is: Don't fix it if it ain't broken.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||02-22-2001||12:37 AM||||Select "run..." from the Start menu.  Type in Regedit.  Select "Export Registry File" from the "Registry" menu in the Registry Editor.  The export range should default on All, but if it's not select all.  Then type in a file name like "registry backup" and hit save.  Could take awhile, depending on how much stuff you have in there.||||reg||1
Z||000003||SteveJ||02-22-2001||08:56 AM||||I used to make my living from fixing computers form guys who "want to get the maximum performance " <BR>Don't screw with it.<BR>I don't know what version of windows you are running but they used to have a utility on the distribution disk called cfgback.exe.<BR>Do a file find on your original cd disk to see if you have it. Program is self explainatory.<BR>And again, if it ain't broke, don't fix it. <BR>(do run scandisk and defrag regularly though)||||reg||1
